// Stricter typecheck config for the frontend app — enables `noImplicitAny`
// and `strictNullChecks` on top of `tsconfig.app.json`. NOT used by Vite
// (that still consumes tsconfig.app.json so the build keeps working);
// only consumed by `scripts/gen-frontend-typecheck-baseline.mjs` to count
// remaining strict-mode violations.
//
// Why a separate config: the frontend has ~900 legacy implicit-any +
// nullability sites. Enabling strict directly in tsconfig.app.json would
// break the build today. The separate config lets us:
//   - Keep production build green
//   - Track strict-mode debt as a monotone-decreasing baseline
//   - Catch any PR that ADDS new strict-mode violations (gate fails)
//   - Migrate incrementally: each PR that touches a hook / page can fix
//     a chunk of its strict errors + regenerate the baseline lower
//
// Long-term goal: when baseline hits 0, tsconfig.app.json adopts the same
// strict settings and this file becomes redundant.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noImplicitAny": true,
    "strictNullChecks": true
  }
}
